(3542449, 494632, 39184, '<td valign="top">Good focus with the motion blur background.  His coat tails flying also lends to the sense of speed here.  He definitely looks like he is enjoying himself.</td>', 'Good focus with the motion blur background.  His coat tails flying also lends to the sense of speed here.  He definitely looks like he is enjoying himself.', '2007-04-12 10:48:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(3542453, 495044, 39184, '<td valign="top">Very creative choice of subject.</td>', 'Very creative choice of subject.', '2007-04-12 10:50:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(3542459, 496087, 39184, '<td valign="top">Wow, regarding the extreme colors.  I''m sorry if I''m off base here, but it seems that something was boosted a little too much here, maybe the contrast or saturation.  The clothes grabs my attention immediately and holds it a little too long for the ''Bicycles'' challenge.  But it is good to see an attempt at something different.</td>', 'Wow, regarding the extreme colors.  I''m sorry if I''m off base here, but it seems that something was boosted a little too much here, maybe the contrast or saturation.  The clothes grabs my attention immediately and holds it a little too long for the ''Bicycles'' challenge.  But it is good to see an attempt at something different.', '2007-04-12 10:55:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(3542463, 493739, 74804, '<td valign="top">awesome cutout!!!!! beautiful shot and I love love love the red! thats a 10!!!</td>', 'awesome cutout!!!!! beautiful shot and I love love love the red! thats a 10!!!', '2007-04-12 10:58:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(3542470, 495959, 74804, '<td valign="top">would have gone black and white on this one, though the colors are great as well</td>', 'would have gone black and white on this one, though the colors are great as well', '2007-04-12 11:02:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(3542472, 496139, 39184, '<td valign="top">Now here is something different.  Good job with the black and white showing just how greasy and grimy the rear sprocket can be.</td>', 'Now here is something different.  Good job with the black and white showing just how greasy and grimy the rear sprocket can be.', '2007-04-12 11:03:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(3542483, 495178, 39184, '<td valign="top">I''m sure that you are getting a lot of comments admonishing you for the small image size.  To score your best, it is important to submit the photo at the maximum size allowable.  I zoomed in 200% to get the image to a comparable size to the rest of the field.  I didn''t see where the focus is here (maybe because of the zoom though) which also takes it down a little.  On the good side, I like your composition, shooting from the rear of the bike with the front tire turned for a profile view as a backdrop to the rest of the bike.</td>', 'I''m sure that you are getting a lot of comments admonishing you for the small image size.  To score your best, it is important to submit the photo at the maximum size allowable.  I zoomed in 200% to get the image to a comparable size to the rest of the field.  I didn''t see where the focus is here (maybe because of the zoom though) which also takes it down a little.  On the good side, I like your composition, shooting from the rear of the bike with the front tire turned for a profile view as a backdrop to the rest of the bike.', '2007-04-12 11:08:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(3542489, 496058, 72423, '<td valign="top">A simple but effective shot.  Nice composition - perhaps more space above the sign would have added to the effect.</td>', 'A simple but effective shot.  Nice composition - perhaps more space above the sign would have added to the effect.', '2007-04-12 11:11:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(3542493, 495381, 72423, '<td valign="top">Perhaps cropping more off the right hand side would have cut down the blueness of the sky which seems to take your attention away from the subject IMHO</td>', 'Perhaps cropping more off the right hand side would have cut down the blueness of the sky which seems to take your attention away from the subject IMHO', '2007-04-12 11:15:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(3542502, 495635, 72423, '<td valign="top">Classic shot.  Nice but lacking ''wow'' factor. Faster shutter speed would have frozen the wheel which may have made every aspect of the main subject sharp.</td>', 'Classic shot.  Nice but lacking ''wow'' factor. Faster shutter speed would have frozen the wheel which may have made every aspect of the main subject sharp.', '2007-04-12 11:17:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(3542503, 494048, 39184, '<td valign="top">Nice shot, but no hands on what?  You would have us believe that you weren''t holding the handle bars and you weren''t holding the camera.  It will be interesting to see how you pulled this one off.  I like the motion blur and the orientation of the photo.  This gives the image a sense of speed, the feeling of a slight loss of control, and a feeling of dizziness.</td>', 'Nice shot, but no hands on what?  You would have us believe that you weren''t holding the handle bars and you weren''t holding the camera.  It will be interesting to see how you pulled this one off.  I like the motion blur and the orientation of the photo.  This gives the image a sense of speed, the feeling of a slight loss of control, and a feeling of dizziness.', '2007-04-12 11:19:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(3542505, 495290, 72423, '<td valign="top">How''d you do this?  Long exposure? The effect is interesting, but the highlights take your attention away from the main subject.  Another angle may have produced a better result.</td>', 'How''d you do this?  Long exposure? The effect is interesting, but the highlights take your attention away from the main subject.  Another angle may have produced a better result.', '2007-04-12 11:20:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(3542506, 493248, 31403, '<td valign="top">oh the potential here!<br/> <br/>Such a pretty girl and a terrific bike!  But just plopping her in the sun and shooting a snap (cropping the bike awkwardly, blasting highlights, tilted background/lack of background)will hurt this photo.<br/> <br/>No studio?  Find a north facing garage, or a south facing one, ok, just find a garage.  Open the door and there will be places in that garage with the most beautiful soft light - then get something to reflect that light with - posterboard, tin foil wrapped around a board, a white sheet, and bounce some light onto the dark side of her - then maybe something to shade the background behind her from the garage light(just maybe on that, the garage might make it cooler).  Maybe some grease on her?  Maybe a tool in her hand as though she''s working on the bike?  Maybe on the floor looking up at the bike and her sitting on the ground?  Oh the possibilities.<br/> <br/>So get that light soft and directed, then show us from a different angle, show us something more interesting about this scene, and you''ll ribbon!  DPC voters are a sucker for a gimmick, and a bikini girl working on a cool bike in soft light is just such a gimmick.<br/> <br/>I hope that helps.  Most will blast through this photo, make some stupid comment about the "babe" (happens to my model photos all the time) and not say a thing about making the photo better.  <br/> <br/>Cheers.</td>', 'oh the potential here! Such a pretty girl and a terrific bike!  But just plopping her in the sun and shooting a snap (cropping the bike awkwardly, blasting highlights, tilted background/lack of background)will hurt this photo. No studio?  Find a north facing garage, or a south facing one, ok, just find a garage.  Open the door and there will be places in that garage with the most beautiful soft light - then get something to reflect that light with - posterboard, tin foil wrapped around a board, a white sheet, and bounce some light onto the dark side of her - then maybe something to shade the background behind her from the garage light(just maybe on that, the garage might make it cooler).  Maybe some grease on her?  Maybe a tool in her hand as though she''s working on the bike?  Maybe on the floor looking up at the bike and her sitting on the ground?  Oh the possibilities. So get that light soft and directed, then show us from a different angle, show us something more interesting about this scene, and you''ll ribbon!  DPC voters are a sucker for a gimmick, and a bikini girl working on a cool bike in soft light is just such a gimmick. I hope that helps.  Most will blast through this photo, make some stupid comment about the "babe" (happens to my model photos all the time) and not say a thing about making the photo better.   Cheers.', '2007-04-12 11:20:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(3542521, 495872, 39184, '<td valign="top">Great choice of composition showing off the patterns of the bars and seat posts contrasting with the deviation from the patterns in the seat height.  The colors and the stripes work well here too.  Perfection would have been to be able to get this shot without the people and the blue taxi sign in the background.  But we work with what we have.  Nice job.</td>', 'Great choice of composition showing off the patterns of the bars and seat posts contrasting with the deviation from the patterns in the seat height.  The colors and the stripes work well here too.  Perfection would have been to be able to get this shot without the people and the blue taxi sign in the background.  But we work with what we have.  Nice job.', '2007-04-12 11:23:51.000000', NULL, 1),
