(3570346, 495831, 72423, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all who voted - I was at 5.5 for a while, then I started to slip.  Still, I scored better than in my first attempt at a challenge.<br/> <br/>And thanks for the comments.  The bike was not mine - it''s being slowly dismantled round the corner from my house - both mudguards have now gone...<br/> <br/>I actually rested the camera on the ground to get the shot and as I could not see what I was shooting, it took me a few attempts to get something I liked.  I took around 30 pics altogether and I selected the one I thought was most effective.  I went the b/w route to give the image more ''mood''.</td>', 'Thanks to all who voted - I was at 5.5 for a while, then I started to slip.  Still, I scored better than in my first attempt at a challenge. And thanks for the comments.  The bike was not mine - it''s being slowly dismantled round the corner from my house - both mudguards have now gone... I actually rested the camera on the ground to get the shot and as I could not see what I was shooting, it took me a few attempts to get something I liked.  I took around 30 pics altogether and I selected the one I thought was most effective.  I went the b/w route to give the image more ''mood''.', '2007-04-22 11:56:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3570641, 495897, 23098, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the feedback.  All comments were appreciated.</td>', 'Thanks for the feedback.  All comments were appreciated.', '2007-04-22 14:26:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(3571585, 495957, 35334, '<td valign="top">I really liked this image and I was disappointed to see how poorly it did in the challenge. This really captures the feeling of riding a bicycle at night. The headlight really just illuminates the bicycle so others can see it; it doesn''t do much to show the road ahead.<br/> <br/>--DanW</td>', 'I really liked this image and I was disappointed to see how poorly it did in the challenge. This really captures the feeling of riding a bicycle at night. The headlight really just illuminates the bicycle so others can see it; it doesn''t do much to show the road ahead. --DanW', '2007-04-22 23:05:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(3571613, 496063, 35334, '<td valign="top">I love this! I''m not sure what is going on here--but that is part of the charm.<br/> <br/>You said on your profile page: "Current thought: I''d like to add more meaning to my photos." I think you have succeeded here. Some people might say that the meaning was in the sculpture you photographed, not something that you added to it. But I think you have added something to it by the way you photographed it.<br/> <br/>--DanW<br/> <br/></td>', 'I love this! I''m not sure what is going on here--but that is part of the charm. You said on your profile page: "Current thought: I''d like to add more meaning to my photos." I think you have succeeded here. Some people might say that the meaning was in the sculpture you photographed, not something that you added to it. But I think you have added something to it by the way you photographed it. --DanW ', '2007-04-22 23:18:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(3571633, 496003, 35334, '<td valign="top">I thought this was a really nice image! I hope the rider is OK.<br/> <br/>--DanW</td>', 'I thought this was a really nice image! I hope the rider is OK. --DanW', '2007-04-22 23:26:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(3574043, 496130, 50674, '<td valign="top">Ég kaus ekki í keppninni og var fyrst að skoða myndir núna. Mér þykir þessi ansi fín og titillinn er góður. Kemur mjög vel út í sv/hv.<br/>Og svo bæti ég við að ég er ósammála einum/einni hér að neðan sem vill meina að það ætti að vera meira pláss/rými kringum hjólin. Þessi skurður gerir mikið fyrir hana og vinir" er svo passandi einmitt þegar þau standa svona þétt og lítið rými í kring.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-04-23 14:49:29.</i></td>', 'Ég kaus ekki í keppninni og var fyrst að skoða myndir núna. Mér þykir þessi ansi fín og titillinn er góður. Kemur mjög vel út í sv/hv.Og svo bæti ég við að ég er ósammála einum/einni hér að neðan sem vill meina að það ætti að vera meira pláss/rými kringum hjólin. Þessi skurður gerir mikið fyrir hana og vinir" er svo passandi einmitt þegar þau standa svona þétt og lítið rými í kring.', '2007-04-23 15:47:28.000000', '2007-04-23 15:49:29.000000', 0),
(3574433, 495826, 17148, '<td valign="top">It was at that moment he questioned if his hat was was SNELL tested and approved.<br/> <br/>Good shot...I agree with the desat...the green would destract.<br/></td>', 'It was at that moment he questioned if his hat was was SNELL tested and approved. Good shot...I agree with the desat...the green would destract.', '2007-04-23 17:53:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3575066, 495819, 47541, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club.<br/> <br/>Fit: There is a bicycle in the shot so its meets challenge.<br/> <br/>Composition: It feels fine, horizon is level, subject isnt centered.  The bike rack on the right distracts a bit from the left of frame where we are supposed to be looking.<br/> <br/>Technical: The longs shadows provide a nice emphasis on the bike.  The mass of brown is a bit bleak feeling.  Increasing the saturation or somehting on the pink may have helped draw the bike out from the browns a bit more (using selective colour not masking)<br/> <br/>Feel: The image doesnt relly spek to me in the way that your notes say you intended.<br/> <br/>PM me if you have any queries.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club. Fit: There is a bicycle in the shot so its meets challenge. Composition: It feels fine, horizon is level, subject isnt centered.  The bike rack on the right distracts a bit from the left of frame where we are supposed to be looking. Technical: The longs shadows provide a nice emphasis on the bike.  The mass of brown is a bit bleak feeling.  Increasing the saturation or somehting on the pink may have helped draw the bike out from the browns a bit more (using selective colour not masking) Feel: The image doesnt relly spek to me in the way that your notes say you intended. PM me if you have any queries.', '2007-04-23 20:55:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3578059, 493600, 55956, '<td valign="top">Greeting from critique club<br/> <br/>Hi, I think that isn''t a bad idea. the composition and the exposure are good. I think that this image have two problems. the first is the background, too much distracting, a better out of focus was better. you can obtain this with the focal length near 55 mm and with the subject near the camera. the second problem is that there isn''t a strong point in the image, there are the bicycles hence the image meet the contest but there isn''t an action or an something that the bikes do.<br/>Sorry for my ugly english :)<br/> <br/>Best Regards<br/>Gennaro</td>', 'Greeting from critique club Hi, I think that isn''t a bad idea. the composition and the exposure are good. I think that this image have two problems. the first is the background, too much distracting, a better out of focus was better. you can obtain this with the focal length near 55 mm and with the subject near the camera. the second problem is that there isn''t a strong point in the image, there are the bicycles hence the image meet the contest but there isn''t an action or an something that the bikes do.Sorry for my ugly english :) Best RegardsGennaro', '2007-04-24 18:58:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3579202, 495035, 10402, '<td valign="top"><b>Greetings from the Critique Club.</b> <br/> <br/>This is a wonderful minimalist photo. Most everything except the shape of the bicycle is stripped away, making the subject very clear. It''s a very dramatic treatment, as was intended. The cobblestones make a great texture with the high contrast; a whole lot more interesting than a smooth road would be.<br/> <br/>The composition is great. It''s nicely balanced and really draws the viewer into the scene. The front hub is right on a rule-of-thirds intersection, and lots of lines point to it, making it the clear focal point. Cutting off the top of the rider intensifies the focus on the bicycle. Cutting off parts of the back wheel is unusual, and it works very well.<br/> <br/>I am bothered by the "missing" spokes. It really isn''t that distracting, and the subject is still clear. It just seems a bit strange to see some spokes but not all of them.<br/> <br/>But overall a great photo. I''ve really enjoyed studying it.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club.  This is a wonderful minimalist photo. Most everything except the shape of the bicycle is stripped away, making the subject very clear. It''s a very dramatic treatment, as was intended. The cobblestones make a great texture with the high contrast; a whole lot more interesting than a smooth road would be. The composition is great. It''s nicely balanced and really draws the viewer into the scene. The front hub is right on a rule-of-thirds intersection, and lots of lines point to it, making it the clear focal point. Cutting off the top of the rider intensifies the focus on the bicycle. Cutting off parts of the back wheel is unusual, and it works very well. I am bothered by the "missing" spokes. It really isn''t that distracting, and the subject is still clear. It just seems a bit strange to see some spokes but not all of them. But overall a great photo. I''ve really enjoyed studying it.', '2007-04-25 00:42:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3580474, 495790, 76778, '<td valign="top">Thanks ExtimaltedEyes, headed out to Death Valley on Geo 18 for the weekend, hope to catch some good shots!</td>', 'Thanks ExtimaltedEyes, headed out to Death Valley on Geo 18 for the weekend, hope to catch some good shots!', '2007-04-25 07:28:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(3581432, 495676, 51538, '<td valign="top">I like the position of the bike in the frame.  It suggests the potential of somewhere to go, and therefore emphasizes the title.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-04-25 12:20:38.</i></td>', 'I like the position of the bike in the frame.  It suggests the potential of somewhere to go, and therefore emphasizes the title.', '2007-04-25 12:40:49.000000', '2007-04-25 13:20:38.000000', 0),
(3582506, 496087, 64352, '<td valign="top">I really expected this shor to do better... it just has such a classic look to it.</td>', 'I really expected this shor to do better... it just has such a classic look to it.', '2007-04-25 17:07:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3587151, 493248, 51793, '<td valign="top">okay let me re-comment on this picture.<br/> <br/>Take what everyone told you and lets look at it in retrospect. <br/> <br/>shannylee13 says: that the grass in the back ground is dead looking and doesnt quite live up to the subject.<br/> <br/>awelsh says: That she is a Nice <b>model</b>, "pandering to male vote", (gee I wonder why he would say that). Not much connection to bikes tho, and she looks like a model on a bike, not like someone who''d actually ride such a bike. - How many women would actually ride a bike in a bikini? A lot you''re thinking, but are they on grass or at the beach??? If you had a beach background this picture would be much better. <br/> <br/>geinafets says: something about the background (which I have already covered). <br/> <br/>Here''s my thoughts. Her facial expression doesn''t match the fact that she is on a bike in the middle of a dead grass field with her hat so low that you can''t see her face detail and the sun is so bright that it''s only showing off one side of her body. <br/> <br/>If I would have taken this picture I would have taken it at the beach or a sidewalk area where someone would actually be riding a bike so it fits the subject a bit more. I would have her remove the hat and put some pants on or something like some cargo jeans. I wouldn''t have her in a bikini bottom. Something a bit more realistic. I would also wait for the sun to go down a bit more or take the picture say around noon when the sun is really high or just about gone. Depending on the light or dark effect you want. Earlier in the day the more darker her face would have been if she was wearing the hat. Later in the day would give a more lighting effect on the entire subject.<br/> <br/>Another good tip is if your subject or your main focal point is going to be something like the color red, have your model put on some red polish and lipstick. For guys it''s good to use something like a chap stick or something to just make them stand out some.  Hope this helps some. Good luck.<br/></td>', 'okay let me re-comment on this picture. Take what everyone told you and lets look at it in retrospect.  shannylee13 says: that the grass in the back ground is dead looking and doesnt quite live up to the subject. awelsh says: That she is a Nice model, "pandering to male vote", (gee I wonder why he would say that). Not much connection to bikes tho, and she looks like a model on a bike, not like someone who''d actually ride such a bike. - How many women would actually ride a bike in a bikini? A lot you''re thinking, but are they on grass or at the beach??? If you had a beach background this picture would be much better.  geinafets says: something about the background (which I have already covered).  Here''s my thoughts. Her facial expression doesn''t match the fact that she is on a bike in the middle of a dead grass field with her hat so low that you can''t see her face detail and the sun is so bright that it''s only showing off one side of her body.  If I would have taken this picture I would have taken it at the beach or a sidewalk area where someone would actually be riding a bike so it fits the subject a bit more. I would have her remove the hat and put some pants on or something like some cargo jeans. I wouldn''t have her in a bikini bottom. Something a bit more realistic. I would also wait for the sun to go down a bit more or take the picture say around noon when the sun is really high or just about gone. Depending on the light or dark effect you want. Earlier in the day the more darker her face would have been if she was wearing the hat. Later in the day would give a more lighting effect on the entire subject. Another good tip is if your subject or your main focal point is going to be something like the color red, have your model put on some red polish and lipstick. For guys it''s good to use something like a chap stick or something to just make them stand out some.  Hope this helps some. Good luck.', '2007-04-27 00:52:04.000000', NULL, 0),
